# Vendored third-party dataset (ADR-0046) — byte-exact or worthless.
#
# `data/idn-admin-regions/upstream/**` holds files copied verbatim from
# `cahyadsn/wilayah` together with the sha256 of every byte
# (`checksums.sha256`, `manifest.json`, and the test that recomputes both).
# `db/wilayah.sql` upstream uses CRLF line endings while its siblings use LF;
# any EOL normalisation on checkout/commit would silently change those bytes and
# make every recorded checksum wrong — turning a provenance record into a lie
# that reads like a passing gate. Marking the subtree `binary` disables EOL
# normalisation (and diffing) for it entirely.
#
# A future vendored file under this path inherits the rule automatically; it
# never needs its own line here.
data/idn-admin-regions/upstream/** binary
